# Swift Kafka JSON events

Generated Swift 6 package (macOS 13+; Linux system toolchain), using Codable/actors and official librdkafka **2.12.0**.
Sources pin the verified upstream release commit
`2f2208847f7f91eaf54bcbd2cedf5dbb2dd3a3fe`. Install that native toolchain before
building; runtime rejects other versions rather than silently claiming coverage.

On macOS/Linux, obtain the official `confluentinc/librdkafka` v2.12.0 release and
build/install it with `./configure --prefix=/your/native/prefix`, `make`, then
`make install`. Install `pkg-config` and set `PKG_CONFIG_PATH` to that prefix's
`lib/pkgconfig`. Alternatively pass `-Xcc -I/your/native/prefix/include` and
`-Xlinker -L/your/native/prefix/lib` to `swift build`, and configure the native loader
library path. SwiftPM declares the system-library dependency explicitly; it does
not install native packages automatically. Generic brew/apt providers may install
a different version; verify `rd_kafka_version_str()` is exactly `2.12.0`.

```swift
let runtime = KafkaDefaults.connect()
// let delivered = try await SendOrderEvent.send(runtime, payload: payload, headers: headers, key: key)
// let subscription = try await ReceiveOrderEvent.subscribe(runtime)
// let record = try await subscription.receive()
// try await process(record.payload)
// try await subscription.ack(record)
// await subscription.close()
await runtime.close()
```

One operation source per operation, canonical shared models, separate codec,
schema/runtime/subscription and small C ABI bridge. Native AsyncAPI document retained.
Header objects must be closed nonnullable strings; optional keys are nonnullable strings.
Supported bounded Draft7 schema constraints are validated before send/after receipt;
unsupported schema keywords (including pattern, unions, refs and format) reject generation.
Numeric schema bounds are limited to finite magnitudes up to 1e28; runtime numeric
validation uses Foundation Decimal and rejects values outside its representable range.
Native producer idempotence and `acks=all` protect transport retries only; no
application deduplication or transactions. Sends await broker delivery metadata;
cancellation stops waiting and does not retract queued records. Producers cache per
operation client ID. Await outstanding sends before closing producers: close may
purge queued/in-flight messages. Consumer subscriptions have independent lifetimes.
Auto-commit/auto-store off, new groups earliest. Manual `ack(record)` or handler-success
`run` commits after success; failed handlers leave offsets uncommitted. Only one pending
record per subscription. Strict UTF-8/JSON, duplicate keys/headers, null headers and
tombstones reject and poison the subscription; close/reopen for replay. Swift Task
cancellation terminates receive waits. Fixed group override conflicts reject.

Static plaintext Kafka JSON subset only: no generated TLS/SASL, registry, transactions,
automatic handler retries, dead-letter policy or other brokers. Separate Kafka and
HTTP/GraphQL output packages are required.
